<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="99F" seq="003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="0" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-99f-003-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Usage Guide</title>
<topic>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Refer to TABLE OF CONTENTS to find the applicable
maintenance procedures or other data.</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para><refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-24-19-1"></refint> gives the function, primary components,
operation and properties of the Double Seat Assembly.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para><refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-24-19-1000"></refint> gives test and fault isolation
procedures.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para><refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-24-19-2000"></refint> gives wiring diagrams illustration.
</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para><refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-24-19-3000"></refint> gives special procedures to
disassemble the Double Seat Assembly for the repair or part replacement.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para><refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-24-19-4000"></refint> gives procedures to clean the
components of the Double Seat Assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para><refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-24-19-5000"></refint> gives procedures to examine
parts for worn areas and damage.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para><refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-24-19-6000"></refint> gives procedures to replace
potted inserts, replace bonded components and make repairs.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para><refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-24-19-7000"></refint> gives special procedures to
assemble the Double Seat Assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para><refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-24-19-8000"></refint> contains assembly torque limits
for screws and nuts.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para><refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-24-19-9000"></refint> gives the recommended special
tools, fixtures, test equipment and consumable materials used in this
manual.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para><refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="ipl-25-24-19"></refint> gives
the data necessary to get replacement parts. An equipment index, a
numerical index and illustrations refer to the parts lists that find
and identify the parts. The INTRODUCTION gives more data.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The sections contain a table of recommended
tools and materials, when applicable. Use equivalent items if necessary.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The procedures in this manual follow the
specifications utilized during production and are thereby shop verified.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
