<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" pgblknbr="1" chg="r"
key="pgblk-25-24-19-1" revdate="20260918"><?Pub Dtl>
<chgdesc>Updated to reflect the new logo and name of the company.</chgdesc>
<chgdesc>Updated manufacturer's name.</chgdesc>
<chgdesc>Updated velcro to hook or loop tape.</chgdesc>
<title>DESCRIPTION AND OPERATION</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="870" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-870-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Description</title>
<topic>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The First Class Double Seat Assembly is shown
in Figure <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="graphic-25-24-19-870-001-a01"></refint>.
The Seat Assembly is mounted to the seat tracks with track fittings
and anti-rattle stud assemblies. The Seat Assembly is equipped with
a base frame assembly, two back structure assemblies, two armcap assemblies,
a center armcap assembly, two in-arm table assemblies, audio jacks,
two PCU, a PC power outlet, two video monitor installation, a IFE
installation, two coat hook assembly, Y-lap belt assemblies, literature
pocket, bottom cushion, back cushion and back dress cover. Several
lap belt extensions are supplied for each aircraft ship set. The recline
actuators control the recline seat positions and are factory set for
the upright and full recline limits. The recline actuator buttons
are located on both the outboard and aisle armrest. The recline position
can be adjusted by the passenger within the range of travel set at
the factory.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The base frame assembly provides installation
of the back structure assemblies, the armcap assemblies and the in-arm
table assemblies. The base frame assembly is equipped with the wall
baggage bar, the track fittings, the anti-rattle stud assemblies,
the outboard leg, four spreader assemblies and two tube assemblies.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The back structure assemblies is constructed
of composite materials for strength and light weight. <revst>Hook
or loop tape<revend> are bonded to the structure to secure the back
dress cover assembly, literature pocket and back scutcheon. The quadrants
are mounted to the bottom corners of the welded back structure and
are connected to the recline actuator and bottom structure assembly.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The center armcap assembly is constructed
of molded and bonded plastic, painted to match the seat exterior.
The armcap assembly is mounted to the top of the armcap structure
and acts as a cushion.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The outboard and aisle armcap assemblies
are constructed of molded and bonded plastic, painted to match the
airline requirements. A spring-loaded catch is provided to secure
the armcap assembly in the lowered position.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The in-arm table assembly is mounted under
the armcap assembly. The in-arm table assembly is attached to the
stanchion assembly of the base frame assembly with a pin.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The bottom cushion, back cushion and literature
pocket are attached to the seat with <revst>hook or loop tape<revend> and
mechanical snaps. The cushion cover color and material are provided
to meet the specifications of the airline.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<?Pub _newpage>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="870" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-870-002-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Operation</title>
<topic>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>To recline the seat, push the recline button
on the armrest and lean back in the seat. To move the seat to the
full upright position, lean forward in the seat and push the recline
button. The seat will move forward when the recline button is pushed.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>To deploy the in-arm table assembly, raise
the armcap assembly, extract the in-arm table assembly from the table
housing and spread out the table trays. To replace the in-arm table
assembly, fold up the trays, insert the in-arm table assembly in the
outboard table housing and close the outboard armcap assembly.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="870" seq="003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1" chg="u"
