<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" pgblknbr="1000" chg="r"
key="pgblk-25-24-19-1000" revdate="20260918"><?Pub Dtl>
<chgdesc>Updated to reflect the new logo and name of the company.</chgdesc>
<title>TESTING AND FAULT ISOLATION</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="99F" seq="016"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-99f-016-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Introduction</title>
<topic>
<title>General</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>This section contains test and fault isolation
procedures. The tests can be done on or off the aircraft.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If a failure occurs during a test, refer
to Fault Isolation Procedures to identify the trouble, possible cause
and corrective action.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Table<refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="table-25-24-19-94c-001-a01"></refint> gives the recommended
test equipment and materials.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Figure <grphcref
refid="sheet-25-24-19-750-001-a01-1"></grphcref> gives the wiring
diagram.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Do the testing and fault isolation procedures
a minimum of one time for year.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Do a check of the flotation cushions at each
3 years after the manufacturing date.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="94C" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1000" id="table-25-24-19-94c-001-a01">
<title>Test Equipment and Materials</title>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="col1">
<colspec colname="col2">
<colspec colname="col3">
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Nomenclature</para>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Part or Specification Number</para>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Source (CAGE)*</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Digital Multi-meter</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Model 75III <?Pub _bookmark Command="[Quick Mark]">or equivalent</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Fluke Corp. (V89536)</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry namest="col1" nameend="col3"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>(1)* Refer to <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="vendlist-25-24-19"></refint>,
for vendor information.</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="700" seq="003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-700-003-a01" revdate="20080417"><?Pub _bookmark
Command="[Quick Mark]">
<title>Electrical Test Procedures</title>
<topic>
<title>Continuity Test</title>
<warning><para>TO PREVENT ELECTRICAL SHOCK OR DAMAGE, DISCONNECT ALL
SOURCES OF ELECTRICAL POWER BEFORE YOU INSTALL OR REMOVE Seat ASSEMBLY.
MAKE SURE THAT A PERSON APPROVED TO USE MODERN METHODS OF FIRST AID
AND RESUSCITATION IS ALWAYS NEAR YOU.</para></warning>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Use a digital multi-meter to make sure point-to-point
continuity of all electrical circuits. Make sure all connections.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Refer to <refint reftype="pgblk-25-24-19-2000"
refid="pgblk-25-24-19-2000"></refint> to do the electrical connections.</para><?Pub
_bookmark Command="[Quick Mark]"></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<?Pub _newpage>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="700" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-700-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Test Procedure</title>
<topic>
<title>Foodtable Assembly Tests</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Open armcap installation.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Lift out in-arm table assembly from table
housing.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Open in-arm table assembly.</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Armcap assembly must easily open.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Table assembly must easily be removed from
table housing.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Table assembly must easily be opened.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Close in-arm table assembly. </para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Insert in-arm table assembly in table housing.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Close armcap installation.</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Table assembly must easily be closed.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Table assembly must easily be installed in
table housing.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Armcap assembly must easily be closed.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Y-Lap Belt Assembly Test</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Fit belt clip in the belt catch.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Belt catch must lock the Y-lap belt positively.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>With a quick jolt, pull on belts to ensure
that belt does not slip through belt catch.</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Belt catch must lock the Y-lap belt.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Lift belt release and separate belt clip
from belt catch.</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Belt catch must unlock and release belt clip
without difficulty.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Seat Recline Test</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Press recline button, then move back structure
assemblies through the entire recline travel range.</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Motion must be free and without binding.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>From the recline position, press and hold
recline button and allow back structure assemblies to rise to the
full upright position.</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Back structure assembly must move freely
to full upright position.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Recline actuator and recline cable must not
bind.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>From the full upright position, press and
hold recline button and move back structure assemblies to the full
recline position. Release recline button.</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Back structure assembly must move smoothly
and positively into full recline position.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Back structure assembly must remain securely
locked in full recline position.</para>
<note><para>Full recline must be 28.8 in. (73.15 cm) from vertical
reference (Refer to figure <refint reftype="pgblk-25-24-19-2000"
refid="graphic-25-24-19-700-001-a01"></refint>).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>From the full recline position, press and
hold recline button and move back structure assemblies to the full
upright position. Release recline button.</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Back structure assembly must move smoothly
and positively into full upright position.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Back structure assembly must remain securely
locked in full upright position.</para>
<note><para>Full upright position must be 23.4 in. (59.43 cm) from
vertical reference (Refer to figure <refint
reftype="pgblk-25-24-19-2000" refid="graphic-25-24-19-700-001-a01"></refint>).
</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Press and hold recline button and move back
structure assemblies to a mid-point in the recline travel. Release
recline button. Push on back structure assemblies to check that back
structure is locked in the desired position.</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Back structure assembly must remain securely
locked in the selected recline position.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
<graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="700" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1000" chg="u"
key="graphic-25-24-19-700-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Full Upright Position and Full Recline Position</title>
<sheet gnbr="I-252419-01001-1-1" sheetnbr="1" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-24-19-700-001-a01-1" revdate="20080417"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
<topic>
<title>Seat-Bottom Cushion Flotation Test</title>
<note><para>This test is only applicable to seat assemblies supplied
with seat-bottom flotation cushions.</para></note>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Randomly collect one flotation cushion from
the cushions with the oldest manufacturing dates. Then, do a buoyancy
test of flotation cushion per TSO-C72c.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The flotation cushion must obey a minimum
buoyancy force of 14 lb (6,35 kg).</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="810" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-810-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Fault Isolation</title>
<topic>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Table <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="table-25-24-19-810-001-a01"></refint> gives the fault isolation
procedures.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="810" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="1000" id="table-25-24-19-810-001-a01">
<title>Fault Isolation Procedures</title>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="col1">
<colspec colname="colspec0" colwidth="1.00*">
<colspec colname="col2">
<thead>
<row>
<entry align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Trouble</para>
</entry>
<entry align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Probable Cause</para>
</entry>
<entry align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Corrective Action</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry morerows="1" valign="middle" align="center">
<para>IFE does not continuity</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Disconnected electrical connector.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Examine all electrical connections for safe contact.</para>
<para>Refer to Figure <grphcref refid="graphic-25-24-19-750-001-a01"></grphcref> for
wiring diagrams.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Damaged Wiring Harness </para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace.</para>
<para>Refer to Figure <grphcref refid="graphic-25-24-19-750-001-a01"></grphcref> for
wiring diagrams.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Armcap binds or does not open.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Bent or broken armcap installation.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace armcap assembly.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>In-arm table assembly binds or cannot be Remove the from foodtable
housing.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Bent or broken spring pin.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace spring pin.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>In-arm table assembly trays bind or cannot be opened.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Bent or broken pins or hinges.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace pins or hinges.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para> lap belt catch does not catch or release belt clip.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Damaged lap belt assembly mechanism.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace lap belt assembly.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para> lap belt catch does not lock on belt when pulled quickly.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Damaged lap belt assembly mechanism.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace lap belt assembly.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="3">
<para>Back structure assembly binds along recline travel or does not
recline.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Damaged recline actuator.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace recline actuator.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Recline cable assembly not properly connected to recline actuator.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Reconnect recline cable assembly.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Damaged recline cable assembly.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace recline cable assembly.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Back structure assembly movement is obstructed by a foreign
object.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Remove the obstruction.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="1">
<para>Back structure assembly does not lock in desired position.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Damaged recline cable assembly.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace recline cable assembly.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Damaged recline actuator.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace recline actuator.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Back structure assembly is not set to correct full recline or
full upright settings.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Recline actuator requires adjustment.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Refer to <refint reftype="pgblk-25-24-19-7000"
refid="pgblk-25-24-19-7000"></refint> to adjust back structure assemblies
full recline and full upright settings.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Flotation cushion does not meet minimum buoyancy force of 14
lbs (6,35 kg).</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Loss of buoyancy force in bottom cushion assembly (15).</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace bottom cushion assembly.</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
</pgblk>
