<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" pgblknbr="3000" chg="r"
key="pgblk-25-24-19-3000" revdate="20260918"><?Pub Dtl>
<chgdesc>Updated to reflect the new logo and name of the company.</chgdesc>
<chgdesc>Updated velcro to hook or loop tape.</chgdesc>
<chgdesc>Updated disassembly procedures.</chgdesc>
<title>DISASSEMBLY</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="99F" seq="007"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-99f-007-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>General Information</title>
<topic>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>This section contains instructions to disassemble
the first class double seat assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>To use this section, first refer to <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="pgblk-25-24-19-1000"></refint> and <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="pgblk-25-24-19-5000"></refint> to identify
the damaged and worn parts. Disassemble the unit only as far as necessary
to remove the damaged components.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Refer to <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-24-19-6000"></refint> to replace stripped Helicoil
inserts, repair damaged dress covers and replace bonded caps and <revst>hook
or loop tape<revend>.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>No special tools or fixtures are needed to
disassemble the first class double seat assembly.</para>
<note><para>When removing fasteners (bolts, screws, washers, nuts,
etc.), bag and tag parts for ease of assembly.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="940" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-940-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Materials and Tools</title>
<topic>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="94A" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-94a-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Consumable Materials</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>No consumable materials are needed for these
disassembly procedures.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="94B" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-94b-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Special Tools</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>No special tools are needed for these disassembly
procedures.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="000" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-000-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Disassembly Procedures</title>
<topic>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="000" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="3000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-000-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>First Class Seat Assembly Disassembly</title>
<caution><para>the seat assembly has covers that are easily damaged.
cover the surfaces and handle the unit with care to prevent damage.</para>
</caution>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the First Class Double Seat assembly
as follows (<revst>1-1 and 1-1A<revend>):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bottom upholstered assembly (10)
from seat bottom assemblies (445 and 440).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the back upholstered assembly (25)
from back structure assemblies (535 and 530).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the headrest assembly
(40) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the headrest dress cover (-45) from
headrest structure assembly (65).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the side cushion (55 and 50) from
headrest structure assembly (65).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the center cushion (60) from headrest
structure assembly (65).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the headrest structure
assembly (65) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Remove the slide block (70) from headrest
structure assembly (65) by removing screws (75), washers (80) and
ball plungers (85) as follows: </para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Remove the hinge assemblies (90) from side
panel assemblies (110 and 105) and center panel assemblies (115) by
removing screws (95) and washers (100).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the coat hook assemblies (120) from
coat hook mounting block assemblies (130) by removing screws (125).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the coat hook mounting block assemblies
(130) from back structure assemblies (535 and 530) by removing screws
(135) and washers (140).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the literature pocket assemblies (145)
from back structure assemblies (535 and 530) by removing screws (150)
and washers (155).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the video monitor
installation (175) as follows (<revst>2-1 and 2-1A<revend>): </para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove monitor shroud assembly (5) from back
structure assemblies (535 and 530, IPL Figure 1) by removing screws
(10, IPL Figure 2) and washers (15).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove monitor bracket assembly (30) from
monitor mount bracket assemblies (100 and 95, IPL Figure 6) by removing
screws (35, IPL Figure 2) and washers (40).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove monitor dummy assembly (45) or SVDU
(45A) from monitor bracket assembly (30) by removing screws (50) and
washers (55).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove monitor bezel (60) from monitor dummy
assembly (45) or SVDU (45A) by removing screws (65) and washers (70).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble double seat assembly
IFE installation (<revst>3-1 and 3-1A<revend>) as follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disconnect A/C outlet unit (5) from forward
center shroud (800, IPL Figure 1).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Release double&nbsp;PC power cable assembly
(15, IPL Figure 3) from base frame assembly (1035, IPL Figure 1).</para>
<note><para>Disconnect double&nbsp;PC power cable assembly (15, IPL
Figure 3) and cable wrap (10) from PC power outlet installation (370,
IPL Figure 1) and interface bracket assembly (790).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disconnect USB cable (25, IPL Figure 3) from
USB coupler (30) and SVDU.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove USB coupler (30) from video monitor
installation (175, IPL Figure 1) by removing screws (35, IPL Figure
3).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble double wire harness
installations (-40 or -40A) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Remove <revst>tapes<revend> conduits (50
or -50A) from back structure assemblies (535 and 530, IPL Figure 1).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Release double IFE cable assembly (55, IPL
Figure 3) from base frame assembly (1035, IPL Figure 1) and back structure
assemblies (535 and 530) by removing cable ties (60, IPL Figure 3).</para>
<note><para>Disconnect double IFE cable assembly (55) and cable wrap
(45) from audio jack assembly (85) and SVDU.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Remove plastic edging grommets (75) from
back structure assemblies (535 and 530, IPL Figure 1).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove audio jack assemblies (85 and 80,
IPL Figure 3) from inner shrouds (855 and 850, IPL Figure 1).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Release PCU cable assembly (90, IPL Figure
3) from base frame assembly (1035, IPL Figure 1) and back structure
assemblies (535 and 530) by removing cable ties (95, IPL Figure 3).</para>
<note><para>Disconnect PCU cable assembly (90) and cable wrap (100)
from SVDU and DPCU.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the back dress cover assemblies (185,
IPL Figure 1) from back structure assemblies (535 and 530).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the lap belt assemblies (195) and
seat belt cover assemblies (190) from seat belt studs (20, IPL Figures
8 and 9).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble the outboard and aisle
armcap installation (240 and 200, IPL Figure 1) as follows: </para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the armcap assemblies (245 and 205)
from outboard and aisle hinged arm trims (580 and 575) by removing
bolts (250 and 210).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the hinge tabs (<revst>255A<revend>,
255, <revst>215A<revend> and 215) from armcap assemblies (245 and
205) by removing setscrews (265 and 225), hinge pins (270 and 230)
and spring torsions (275 and 235).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the center armcap assembly (280 or
280A) from center arm trims (640 and 635) by removing screws (285)
and washers (290).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove bezel closeout PCU (295) from center
armcap assembly (280 or 280A).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove tab (300) from bezel closeout PCU
(295) by removing screws (305) and washers (310).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove  the outboard and aisle escutcheon
(<revst>315 <revend>and 315A) from base frame assembly (1035) by removing
screws (325).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the center escutcheon (330) from base
frame assembly (1035) by removing screws (335).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the outboard and aisle aft armcap
assemblies (<revst>340A<revend> and 340) from base frame assembly
(1035) by removing screw (350).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the center aft armcap assembly (355)
from base frame assembly (1035) by removing screws (365 and 360).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove PC power provisions outlet installation
(370) from base frame assembly (1035) and outboard forward shroud
(745) by removing screws (390) and washers (395).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble PC power provisions outlet installation
(370) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove power outlet bezel (375) from bracket
bezel mount (385) by removing rivets (-380).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove and disassemble audio jack installation
(400) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para><?Pub _bookmark Command="[Quick Mark]">Remove
audio jack bracket assembly (405) from base frame assembly (1035)
by removing screws (410) and washers (415).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove audio plug (420) from audio jack bracket
assembly (405).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove  the in-arm table assemblies (430
and 425) from base frame assembly (1035) by removing pins (<revst>-426
and<revend> 435).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the in-arm table assemblies (430
and 425) as follows (<revst>4-1 thru 4-1C<revend>):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the foodtable pivot assembly (<revst>5
thru -5C<revend>) from foodtable support assembly (<revst>40 thru
-40C<revend>) by removing setscrew (10) and pin (15).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the helicoil (-30 and -31), bushing
(25) and tray insert (20) from foodtable pivot (<revst>35 and -35A)
and pivot fitting (-36 and -36A)<revend>.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the foodtable support assembly (<revst>40thru
-40C<revend>) from sliding table (<revst>70 thru -70C<revend>) by
removing screws (45).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the slide guides (60), <revst>washer
(-61)<revend> and slides (50) from support (<revst>65 thru -65C<revend>)
by removing screws (55).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the sliding table (<revst>70 thru
-70C<revend>) from table (85 or -85A) by removing <revst>setscrew
(-74)<revend> pins (75) and hinges (80).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disconnect the cable assembly (660, IPL Figure
1) from recline actuator (510) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Release cable assemblies (660) from base
frame assembly (1035) as shown in Figure <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="graphic-25-24-19-440-005-a01"></refint> by removing cable ties
(665).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Disconnect lock clips of the cable assemblies
(660) from recline actuators (510).</para>
<note><para>Removing nuts (450), washers (455) and bolts (465 and
460) will also disconnect recline actuator (510) from back structure
assemblies (535 and 530).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the seat bottom assemblies (445 and
440) from base frame assembly (1035), back structure assemblies (535
and 530) and recline actuator (510) by removing nuts (450), washers
(455) and bolts (465 and 460).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the seat bottom assemblies (445
and 440) as follows (<revst>5-1 and 5-1A<revend>):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the track guides (5) from spreaders
(55 and 60) by removing screws (10).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the seat bottom stop assembly (15)
from rear tube assemblies (35 or -35A) by removing nuts (20), washers
(25) and screws (30).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the rear tube (35 or -35A) from spreaders
(55 and 60) by removing screws (40).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the tubes (45) from spreaders (55
and 60) by removing screws (50).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the spreaders (55 and 60) from seat
bottom panel (75) by removing rivets (65) <revst>and washer (-65)
as follows:<revend></para></prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para><revst>Remove the bushings (-67) from the
spreader structures.</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Remove the nutplates (-68) from the spreader
structures by removing rivets (-69 and -69A) and spreader (-70 or
-70A)<revend></para></prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the <revst>hook tape<revend> (71)
from seat bottom pan (75).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove  the life vest pouch assemblies (470,
IPL Figure 1) from life vest pan (490) by removing nuts (475), washers
