<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the foodtable guides assemblies (1025)
from armrest panels (940 and 890) by removing rivets (-1030).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Disassemble the base frame assembly (1035)
as follows (<revst>7-1<revend>):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the wall baggage bar (5) as follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the wall baggage bar (5) from baggage
bar splice assembly (85) by removing pin (10).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the wall baggage bar (5) from T bracket
(50) and the baggage bar attach plate (30) by removing nuts (15),
washers (20) and screws (25).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the T bracket (50) and the baggage
bar attach plate (30) from front tube assembly (415) by removing nuts
(35), washers (40) and bolts (45).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the aisle baggage bar (55) as follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove aisle baggage bar (55) from baggage
bar attach bracket assembly (75) by removing screws (60).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove aisle baggage bar (55) from baggage
bar splice assembly (85) by removing screw (65) and washer (70).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the baggage bar attach bracket assembly
(75) from aisle spreader assembly (185) by removing screw (80).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the baggage bar splice assembly (85)
from leg (255) by removing screw (90) and washer (95) <revst>as follows:<revend></para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para><revst>Remove the helicoil inserts (-96)
from the baggage bar splice structure.<revend></para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the slide assemblies (100) from spreader
assemblies (395, 390, 340 and 185).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the support bumper assembly (105)
from aisle stanchion assembly (155) and from aisle spreader assembly
(185) by removing screws (115 and 110) <revst>as follow:<revend></para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para><revst>Remove the helicoil inserts (-116)
from the baggage bar splice structure.<revend></para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the aisle bracket assembly (120) from
aisle stanchion assembly (155) by removing screws (125) and washers
(130).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the outboard and aisle pusher assemblies
(140 and 135) from outboard and aisle stanchion assemblies (160 and
155) by removing screws (145) and washers (150).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the outboard and aisle stanchion assemblies
(160 and 155) from outboard and aisle spreader assemblies (340 and
185) by removing screws (165) <revst>as follows:<revend></para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para><revst>Remove the helicoil inserts (-166
thru -168) from the aisle stanchion structure.<revend></para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the center armrest stanchion (170)
from center spreader assemblies (395 and 390) by removing screws (175)&nbsp;and
washers (180).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disconnect aisle spreader assembly (185)
from rear and front tube assemblies (420 and 415) by removing nuts
(190), washers (210 and 195), bolts (200) and screws (205).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the aisle track fitting (215) from
leg (255) by removing cap nut (220), washers (230 and 225), screw
(235) and grommets (240).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove aisle trunnion (250) and aisle anti-rattle
stud assembly (245) from leg (255). </para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para><revst>Remove the setscrew (-251) from the
trunion assembly.<revend></para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the leg (255) from rear and front
tube assemblies (420 and 415) by removing nuts (260), washers (265)
and bolts (275 and 270).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove outboard trunnion (285) and outboard
anti-rattle stud assembly (280) from forward fitting adapter (370).</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para><revst>Remove the setscrew (-286) from the
trunion assembly.<revend></para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the outboard track fitting (290) from
aft fitting adapter assembly (315) by removing bolt (295), washers
(305 and 300) and grommets (310).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the aft fitting adapter assembly (315)
from outboard spreader assembly (340) by removing nut (320), bolts
(330 and 325) and washers (335).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disconnect spreader assembly (340) from rear
and front tube assemblies (420 and 415) by removing nuts (345),  washers
(365 and 350), screws (360) and bolts (355).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the outboard and aisle spreader
assemblies (340 and 185) as follows (<revst>8-1 and 8-1A<revend>):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the pivot arm (<revst>-5 thru -5C<revend>)
from aisle or outboard spreader (80 or -80A) by removing screws (10), <revst>bolt
(11), nut (12), spacers (13 or -13A) <revend>and helicoils (15).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the seat belt studs (20) and spacers
(25) from aisle or outboard spreader (80 or -80A).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the shaft assembly (30) from aisle
or outboard spreader (80 or -80A) by removing setscrew (35) and helicoil
(40).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove <revst>loop tape<revend> (50) from
the rubatex bumper (45).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the nut plate (55) from aisle or outboard
spreader (80 or -80A) by removing rivets (60).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the helicoils (75,70 and 65) from
aisle or outboard spreader (80 or -80A).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the forward outboard fitting adapter
(370, IPL Figure 7) from outboard spreader assembly (340).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bottom closeout armrest panels
(380 and 375) from center spreader assemblies (395 and 390) by removing
rivets (-385).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disconnect center spreader assembly (395
and 390) from rear and front tube assemblies (420 and 415) by removing
rivets (-400), screws (405) and washers (410).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Disassemble the center spreader assemblies
(395 and 390) as follows (<revst>9-1 and 9-1A<revend>):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the pivot arm (<revst>-5 thru -6A<revend>)
from center aisle or outboard spreader (65 or -65A) by removing screws
(<revst>-10), bolt (-11), nut (-12), spacers (13 or -13A) and helicoils
(15).<revend></para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the seat belt studs (20) and spacers
(25) from center aisle or outboard spreader (65 or -65A).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the shaft assembly (30) from center
aisle or outboard spreader (65 or -65A) by removing setscrew (35)
and helicoil (40).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the nut plate (45) from center aisle
or outboard spreader (65 or -65A) by removing rivets (50).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove the helicoils (60 and 55) from center
aisle or outboard spreader (65 or -65A).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
</pgblk>
<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" pgblknbr="4000" chg="r"
key="pgblk-25-24-19-4000" revdate="20260918"><?Pub Dtl>
<chgdesc>Updated to reflect the new logo and name of the company.</chgdesc>
<title>CLEANING</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="99F" seq="008"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-99f-008-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>General Information for Cleaning</title>
<topic>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="100" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-100-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>General Information</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<caution><para>the decorative laminate surface of various interior
components can be damaged by the use of incorrect cleaning materials
and equipment or incorrect mixing of the specified cleaning materials. </para>
</caution>
<caution><para>do not use abrasive materials on the decorative surfaces.
do not scrape the surfaces with sharp tools.</para></caution>
<para>This section provides cleaning instructions for the Seat Assembly.
Correct use of the materials and equipment will provide acceptable
cleaning, minimize hazards to personnel and prevent possible damage
to the equipment.</para>
<note><para>The companies that make the cleaning materials can change
the formula. Therefore, always follow the instructions given on the
container. The instructions to mix and use the cleaning materials,
given on the container, supersede the instructions given here.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="940" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-940-002-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Material and Special Tools</title>
<topic>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="94A" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-94a-002-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Consumable Material</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Consumable materials needed for cleaning
are given in Table <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="table-25-24-19-94a-001-a01"></refint>.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="94A" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" id="table-25-24-19-94a-001-a01">
<title>Consumable Materials</title>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="col1">
<colspec colname="col2">
<colspec colname="col3">
<thead>
<row>
<entry align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Material Name and Number</para>
</entry>
<entry align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Source (1)</para>
</entry>
<entry align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Use</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry>
<para>CALLA 301-A LEMON, Detergent, Aqueous Anionic</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Zip - Chem Prod. Inc. (V8E913)</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0">
<para>To clean molded plastic areas, clean metal parts and remove
adhesive.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Cloths, Cotton (clean and dry)</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0">
<para>To apply prepared detergent solutions.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>DEL-12, Cleaner Kit, Leather</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Douglass Interior Products, Inc. (V0HGX6)</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0">
<para>To clean soiled areas.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Detergent, Mild Household</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0">
<para>To clean molded plastic areas.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>P-D-680, Type III, Solvent, Cleaning (optional)</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0">
<para>To clean metal parts.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Solvent, Cleaning (Aliphatic Naphtha) (2)</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0">
<para>To clean metal parts.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Stain Remover, Leather</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Kiss Cleaner and Associate (V0PVV2)</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0">
<para>To remove stains.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>#0166, Lubricant, Silicone </para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Zep Manufacturing Co. (V27674)</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0">
<para>To clean metal parts.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>815MX, Detergent, Aqueous Anionic</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Brulin &amp; Co. (V94058)</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0">
<para>To clean molded plastic areas, clean metal parts and remove
adhesive.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry namest="col1" nameend="col3"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>(1) Refer to <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="vendlist-25-24-19"></refint>,
for vendor information.</para>
<para>(2) Alternate materials. Use Cleaning Solvent only in well-ventilated
areas. Detergents No. 815MX and 1300A are for use in areas that are
not well ventilated or where use of petroleum-based materials is not
allowed or is inadvisable.</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="94B" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-94b-002-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Special Tools</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Table <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="table-25-24-19-94b-001-a01"></refint> gives the recommended
cleaning Special tools.</para>
<note><para>Equivalent substitutes may be used for the items listed.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="94B" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" id="table-25-24-19-94b-001-a01">
<title>Special Tools</title>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="col1">
<colspec colname="col2">
<colspec colname="col3">
<thead>
<row>
<entry align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para> Tool Name and Number</para>
</entry>
<entry align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Source</para>
</entry>
<entry align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Use</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Apron</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
