<para>To protect the body when using solvents and detergents.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Bottle, Spray</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To apply prepared detergent solutions.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Brush, Soft-Bristled </para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To apply prepared detergent solutions.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Gloves, Chemical Resistant</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To protect the hands when using cleaning solvents.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Goggles, Eye Safety </para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To protect the eyes when using cleaning solvents.</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
<?Pub _newpage>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="100" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="4000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-100-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Cleaning Procedures</title>
<topic>
<caution><para>THE DECORATIVE LAMINATE SURFACE OF VARIOUS INTERIOR
COMPONENTS CAN BE DAMAGED BY THE USE OF INCORRECT CLEANING MATERIALS
AND EQUIPMENT or INCORRECT MIXING OF THE SPECIFIED CLEANING MATERIALS.</para>
</caution>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE ABRASIVE MATERIALS ON THE DECORATIVE SURFACES.
DO NOT SCRAPE THE SURFACES WITH SHARP TOOLS.</para></caution>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><title>Molded Plastic Cleaning</title></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use of Mild Household Detergent</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Prepare a solution of mild household detergent
(Table <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-24-19-94a-001-a01"></refint>)
and lukewarm water (approximately 1 part detergent to 50 parts water).
Apply the mild detergent solution with a sponge or a cotton cloth.
Scrub soiled areas and repeat the applications as required to remove
all dirt. Use a soft-bristled brush to clean heavily textured surfaces
or crevices. Rinse the surfaces with clean water to remove the detergent
solution. Dry the surfaces with a clean, dry, cotton cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use of BRULIN 815MX</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>DO NOT USE BRULIN 815MX CLEANER UNDILUTED. SOLUTIONS
STRONGER THAN SPECIFIED CAN DAMAGE THE DECORATIVE SURFACES.</para>
</caution>
<para>Prepare a solution of 1 part BRULIN 815MX (Table <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-24-19-94a-001-a01"></refint>) to
64 parts water for light soil and up to 1 part BRULIN 815MX to 10
parts water for heavy soil. Apply the solution with a spray bottle,
a soft-bristled brush or a cotton cloth. Scrub soiled areas with a
soft-bristled brush or a cotton cloth and repeat the applications
as required to remove any dirt. Wipe the solution off with a clean,
damp, cotton cloth. Dry the surfaces with a clean, dry, cotton cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use of CALLA 301-A LEMON</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Prepare a solution of 1 part CALLA 301-A
LEMON (Table <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="table-25-24-19-94a-001-a01"></refint>) with 4 to 8 parts water
for general cleaning. Use full strength on spots. Apply the solution
with a spray bottle, a soft-bristled brush or a cotton cloth. Allow
time for the solution to penetrate. Scrub soiled areas with a soft-bristled
brush or cotton cloth and repeat the applications as required to remove
all dirt. Wipe the solution off with a clean, damp, cotton cloth.
Dry the surfaces with a clean, dry, cotton cloth.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><title>Metal Part Cleaning</title></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>As a normal routine for cleaning and maintenance,
all metal parts in contact with one another must be lubricated with
silicone lubricant (Table <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="table-25-24-19-94a-001-a01"></refint>) during any shop repair
or at least once every two years.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use of Solvent or Aliphatic Naphtha.</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<warning><para>ALIPHATIC NAPHTHA IS toxic and FLAMMABLE. USE ONLY
IN WELL VENTILATED AREA AND AWAY FROM OPEN FLAME. AVOID PROLONGED
OR REPEATED CONTACT WITH SKIN OR INHALATION OF VAPORS. USE SHOP SAFETY
PRECAUTION FOR HANDLING FLAMMABLE MATERIALS.</para></warning>
<caution><para>DO NOT LET THE ALIPHATIC NAPHTHA CONTACT THE DECOR
MATERIAL OR PLASTIC COMPONENTS. THE NAPHTHA CAN DAMAGE THE COMPONENTS
AND MATERIALS.</para></caution>
<para>Moisten a clean, dry, cotton cloth with cleaning solvent or
Aliphatic Naphtha (Table <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="table-25-24-19-94a-001-a01"></refint>) and wipe the metal parts
clean. Repeat the applications as required to remove all dirt. Dry
the parts with a clean, dry, cotton cloth before solvent evaporates.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use of BRULIN 815 MX</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Prepare a solution of 1 part BRULIN 815MX
(Table <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-24-19-94a-001-a01"></refint>)
to 64 parts water for light soil and up to 1 part BRULIN 815MX to
10 parts water for heavy soil. Apply the solution with a spray bottle,
a soft-bristled brush or a cotton cloth. Scrub soiled areas with a
soft-bristled brush or a cotton cloth. Repeat the applications as
required to remove all dirt. Wipe the solution off with a clean, damp,
cotton cloth. Dry the part with a clean, dry, cotton cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use of CALLA 301-A LEMON</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Prepare a solution of 1 part CALLA 301-A
LEMON (Table <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="table-25-24-19-94a-001-a01"></refint>) with 4 to 8 parts water
for general cleaning. Use full strength for heavy soil and adhesives.
Apply the solution with either a spray bottle, a soft-bristled brush
or a cotton cloth. Allow time for the solution to penetrate. Scrub
soiled areas with a soft-bristled brush or a cotton cloth. Repeat
the applications as required to remove all dirt. Wipe the solution
off with a clean, damp, cotton cloth. Dry the part with a clean, dry,
cotton cloth.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<?Pub _newpage>
<prcitem1><prcitem><title>Adhesive Removal Procedures</title></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use of BRULIN 815MX</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>To remove adhesive tape or adhesive residue,
prepare a solution of 1 part BRULIN 815MX (Table <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-24-19-94a-001-a01"></refint>) to
10 parts water. Moisten a clean cotton cloth with the solution and
wipe the area clean. Repeat the applications as required to remove
all residue. Wipe the solution off with a clean, damp, cotton cloth.
Dry the surface with a clean, dry, cotton cloth.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use of CALLA 301-A LEMON</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>To remove adhesive tape or adhesive residue,
use CALLA 301-A LEMON (Table <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="table-25-24-19-94a-001-a01"></refint>) at full strength. Apply
the solution with a spray bottle, a soft bristled brush or a cotton
cloth. Allow time for the solution to penetrate. Scrub soiled areas
with a soft-bristled brush or a cotton cloth. Repeat the applications
as required to remove all dirt. Wipe the solution off with a clean,
damp, cotton cloth. Dry the surface with a clean, dry, cotton cloth.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><title>Adhesive Removal Procedures</title></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>The recommended fabric cleaning materials
are given in Table <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="table-25-24-19-94a-001-a01"></refint>.</para>
<note><para>Dry cleaning is the preferred method of cleaning the seat
fabric.</para></note>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Vacuum upholstery thoroughly or brush with
a soft-bristle upholstery or clothing brush (Table <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-24-19-94b-001-a01"></refint>).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Remove dry or water - borne soil with concentrated
detergent preparations, commonly called upholstery shampoo. Use recommended
detergent preparations as given in Table <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="table-25-24-19-94a-001-a01"></refint>. Mix upholstery shampoo
as directed on container and apply to a small area (approximately
one square foot) with a small clean brush. Liberal application will
assist in loosening deep-seated dirt.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem>
<caution><para>USE SOLVENT-TYPE CLEANING AGENTS IN WELL-VENTILATED
AREA. AVOID BREATHING SOLVENT VAPORS AND PROLONGED SOLVENT CONTACT
WITH SKIN. USE SHOP SAFETY PRECAUTIONS FOR HANDLING FLAMMABLE MATERIALS.</para>
</caution>
<para>Oil or grease spots are best removed with solvent-type cleaning
agents or with solvent-impregnated powder as given in Table <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-24-19-94a-001-a01"></refint>. Test
material to be cleaned by first applying cleaning agent to a small
area of the material that is not usually visible. Use cleaning agents
sparingly, without saturating fabric, to avoid spotting and damage.
Apply cleaning agent with a clean, soft cloth and avoid spreading
any stains by working from outer edges toward center of stain.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>After using upholstery shampoo or solvent-type
cleaning agent, roll a clean Turkish towel or other absorbent cloth
into a cylindrical shape and wipe off detergent and dirt. Rotate rolled
cloth frequently to present a clean section to the fabric surface. </para>
<note><para>Dirt and soil are absorbed or transferred to the clean
towel by frequently presenting a clean face to the fabric. Vigorous
rubbing may be required to remove soil evenly and to avoid spotting
after drying.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
</pgblk>
<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" pgblknbr="5000" chg="r"
key="pgblk-25-24-19-5000" revdate="20260918"><?Pub Dtl>
<chgdesc>Updated to reflect the new logo and name of the company.</chgdesc>
<title>INSPECTION/CHECK</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="200" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-200-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>GENERAL</title>
<topic>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="200" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-200-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>General Information</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Refer to the Check Procedures to visually
examine the components of the First Class Double Seat Assembly for
damage and wear.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Refer to <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-24-19-6000"></refint> section to repair minor damage.
If the damage is major or beyond simple repair, replace the part.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The inspection/check should be performed
a minimum of once annually.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="210" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-210-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Materials and Tools</title>
<topic>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="94A" seq="003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-94a-003-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Consumable Materials</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>No consumable materials are needed for these
Inspection/Check procedures.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="94B" seq="003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-94b-003-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Special Tools</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>No special tools are needed for these Inspection/Check
procedures.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="200" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-200-002-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Check Procedures</title>
<topic>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="200" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-200-002-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Check Procedures</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Detailed check procedures are given in Table <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-24-19-210-001-a01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="210" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="5000" id="table-25-24-19-210-001-a01">
<title>Check Procedures</title>
<tgroup cols="4">
<?PubTbl tgroup dispwid="7.67in">
<colspec colname="col1" colwidth="0.71*">
<colspec colname="col2" colwidth="0.71*">
<colspec colname="col3" colwidth="0.75*">
<colspec colname="col4" colwidth="1.84*">
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Component</para>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Method of Inspection</para>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Check For</para>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Corrective Action</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry>
<para>All Parts</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Visual</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Cleanliness.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Refer to <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="pgblk-25-24-19-4000"></refint> section
to clean parts.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>All Metal Parts</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Visual</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Nicks, cracks, cuts, scoring, gouges, distortion, corrosion
or other damage which could impair operation.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Repair minor nicks and scratches. Replace damaged parts.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="4">
<para>First Class Double Seat Assembly</para>
<para>(IPL Figure 1)</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="4">
<para>Visual</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Grease, dirt, frays or separations on upholstered bottom cushion
assemblies, upholstered back cushion assemblies, upholstered back
cushion assemblies or literature pocket assemblies; cut, torn or damaged
upholstery.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Refer to <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="pgblk-25-24-19-4000"></refint> to
Remove the grease and dirt; replace if damaged; refer to <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="pgblk-25-24-19-6000"></refint> to repair
damaged seams.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Frayed lap belt assemblies.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Bent, deformed or damaged hydraulic locks; leakage.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Cut, chipped or damaged cart bumpers; deteriorated rubber.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Cut, torn or damaged life vest pouches.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="1">
<para>In-arm Table Assembly</para>
<para>(IPL Figure 4)</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="1">
<para>Visual</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Bent or damaged foodtable pivot.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Check for bent or damaged pin (10). Replace damaged part.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Damaged tables.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Check for bent or damaged pins (55) and hinges (60). Replace
damaged parts.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="6">
<para>Seat Bottom Assembly</para>
<para>(IPL Figure 5)</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="6">
<para>Visual</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Grease, dirt, frays or separations on bottom cushion assembly,
upholstered back cushion assembly, headrest assembly, back dress cover
assembly or literature pocket assembly; cut, torn or damaged upholstery.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Refer to <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="pgblk-25-24-19-4000"></refint> to
Remove the grease and dirt; replace if damaged; refer to <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="pgblk-25-24-19-6000"></refint> to repair
damaged seams.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Frayed lap belt assembly.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Bent, deformed or damaged recline actuators; leakage.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Cut, chipped or damaged cart bumper; deteriorated rubber.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Scratched, gouged or worn armcap assemblies and aft armcap assemblies. 
</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Scratched, gouged or worn escutcheons.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Cracked, deformed or damaged spreaders.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Return bottom seat assembly to manufacturer for repair.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="1">
<para>Back Structure Assembly</para>
<para>(IPL Figure 6)</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="1">
<para>Visual</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Cracked, deformed or damaged quadrants or back pivot brackets.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace damaged parts.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Cracked or damaged welded back structure.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace seat back assembly.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry morerows="5">
<para>Base Frame Assembly</para>
<para>(IPL Figure 7)</para>
</entry>
<entry morerows="5">
<para>Visual</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Bent or damaged baggage bar assembly.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Bent or damaged bracket assembly.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Track fittings do not tighten against seat tracks; damaged or
deformed.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Cracked, damaged or deformed leg.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Damaged or deformed seat belt studs.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Cracked, punctured or damaged diaphragm.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Return base frame assembly to manufacturer for repair.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Spreader Assembly</para>
<para>(IPL Figure 8)</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Visual</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Cut, chipped or damaged cart bumper; deteriorated rubber.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Center Spreader Assembly</para>
<para>(IPL Figure 9)</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Visual</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Cut, chipped or damaged cart bumper; deteriorated rubber.</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Replace.</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
</pgblk>
<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" pgblknbr="6000" chg="r"
key="pgblk-25-24-19-6000" revdate="20260918"><?Pub Dtl>
<chgdesc>Updated to reflect the new logo and name of the company.</chgdesc>
<chgdesc>Added new subtask for rivets.</chgdesc>
<chgdesc>Updated velcro to hook or loop tape.</chgdesc>
<chgdesc>Updated manufacturer's name.</chgdesc>
<title>REPAIR</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="99F" seq="009"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-99f-009-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>General Repair Information</title>
<topic>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="300" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-300-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>General Information</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>This section contains procedures to repair
components of the seat assembly. The repair procedures covered in
this section are given below.</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Upholstery Seam and <revst>Hook or Loop Tape<revend> Repair
(Refer to <refint reftype="subtask-25-24-19-300-002-a01"
refid="subtask-25-24-19-300-002-a01"></refint>).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Replace Threaded Helicoil Inserts (Refer
to <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="subtask-25-24-19-300-003-a01"></refint>).
</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Replace or Install Bonded Components (Refer
to <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="subtask-25-24-19-300-004-a01"></refint>).
</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Touch-up Paint Procedure (Refer to <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="subtask-25-24-19-300-005-a01"></refint>).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Repainting Procedure (Refer to <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="subtask-25-24-19-300-006-a01"></refint>).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Repair of Minor Nicks or Scratches (Refer
to <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="subtask-25-24-19-300-007-a01"></refint>).
</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para><revst>Rivets (Refer to <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="subtask-25-24-19-300-008-a01"></refint>).<revend></para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="94A" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-94a-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Materials and Tools</title>
<topic>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="94A" seq="004"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-94a-004-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Consumable Materials</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The consumable materials needed for repair
are listed in <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="table-25-24-19-94a-002-a01"></refint>.</para>
<note><para>Equivalent substitutes may be used for the items listed.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="94A" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" id="table-25-24-19-94a-002-a01">
<title>Consumable Materials</title>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="col1">
<colspec colname="col2">
<colspec colname="col3">
<thead>
<row>
<entry align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Material Name and Number</para>
</entry>
<entry align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Source</para>
</entry>
<entry align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Use</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry>
<para>A-A-59282, Alcohol, Ethyl</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To clean components prior to repair.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>BZT-69, Thread, Nylon or   V-T-295, Thread, Nylon (Type I, Class
A, Size FF)</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para><revst>Safran Seats USA LLC (V3K723) <revend></para>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To repair upholstery seam and <revst>hook or loop tape<revend>.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Cloths, Cotton (clean and dry)</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To clean components prior to repair.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Cloths, Lint-Free</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To clean components prior to repair.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>DP100, Adhesive</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>3M Co. (V6A669)</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To install <revst>hook or loop tape<revend>.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>Gloss, Chemical Resistant</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To touch up painted surfaces.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>HSH IP, Primer (light gray finish)</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para><revst>Safran Seats USA LLC (V3K723)<revend></para>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To touch-up painted surfaces.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>IP 1065, Paint, Light Gray Top Coat (Color FV3214)</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para><revst>Safran Seats USA LLC (V3K723)<revend></para>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To touch-up painted surfaces.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>IP 1065B, Paint Kit, Touch up, (Color FV3214)</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para><revst>Safran Seats USA LLC (V3K723)<revend></para>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To touch-up painted surfaces.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>HSH IP, Primer (light gray finish)</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para><revst>Safran Seats USA LLC (V3K723)<revend></para>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To touch-up painted surfaces.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>IP 1065, Paint, Light Gray Top Coat (Color FV3214)</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para><revst>Safran Seats USA LLC (V3K723)<revend></para>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To touch-up painted surfaces.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>IP 1065B, Paint Kit, Touch up, (Color FV3214)</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para><revst>Safran Seats USA LLC (V3K723)<revend></para>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To touch-up painted surfaces.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>IP 650ES, Clear Coat</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para><revst>Safran Seats USA LLC (V3K723)<revend></para>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To touch-up painted surfaces.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>MIL-C-38334, Compound, Corrosion Removing</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To remove corrosion.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>MIL-C-5541, Film Chemical (color optional)</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To repair nicks or scratches.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>MIL-P-8585, Primer, Zinc Chromate</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To replace helicoil inserts.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>MIL-T-44010, Thread, Kevlar (#10 30/3 Spun, Natural Color)</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To repair upholstery seam and <revst>hook or loop tape<revend>.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>P-C-451, Cloth, Abrasive (Aluminum Oxide, Medium Grit)</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To replace bonded components.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>P-C-458, Cloth, Crocus</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To repair nicks or scratches.</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
<?Pub _newpage>
</subtask>
