</entry>
<entry>
<para>To replace helicoil inserts.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>3695-3, Tool, Threaded Insert Tang Removal</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Commercially available</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To replace helicoil inserts.</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>
<para>7552-3, Tool, Threaded Insert Installation</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>Emhart Fastening Systems Group (V01566)</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To replace helicoil inserts.</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="300" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-300-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Repair Procedures</title>
<topic>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="300" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-300-002-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Upholstery Seam and <revst>Hook or Loop Tape<revend> Repair</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Repair broken upholstery seams as follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Refer to <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-24-19-4000"></refint> section to clean upholstery.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Select Kevlar or nylon thread with color
and type to match fabric and existing stitches.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Stitch broken seam using same stitch pattern
of a matching seam.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Repair <revst>hook or loop tape<revend> on
seat covers as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Refer to <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="pgblk-25-24-19-4000"></refint> section to clean upholstery.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<caution><para>take care not to pierce or damage the bonded fire blocking
material when repairing damaged stitching on seat covers.</para>
</caution>
<para>Use Kevlar or nylon thread to make necessary minor repairs to
secure any loose parts on the <revst>hook or loop tape<revend> by
hand. Use a curved fisherman&rsquo;s needle. Take care not to pierce
or damage the bonded fire blocking material.</para>
<note><para>Minor repair to loose or damaged stitches can be accomplished
on <revst>hook or loop tape<revend> sewn to seat covers. However,
it is not recommended that the complete replacement or major repair
of <revst>hook or loop tape<revend> be attempted on seat covers. Once
the fire blocking material is bonded to the seat cover material, sewing
by machine is not possible.</para></note>
<note><para>Ensure that <revst>hook or loop tape<revend> are fully
stitched around periphery.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="300" seq="003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-300-003-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Replace Threaded Helicoil Inserts</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove damaged Helicoil inserts with insert
removal tool.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Use a thread gage from tap and die set to
determine correct size of thread chaser.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Use thread chaser from tap and die set to
clean tapped hole and repair any crossed or stripped threads.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>zinc chromate primer is toxic and flammable. use only
in well ventilated area and away from open flame. avoid prolonged
or repeated contact with skin or inhalation of vapors. use shop safety
precaution for handling flammable materials.</para></warning>
<para>Wet the replacement inserts with zinc chromate primer. Use threaded
insert installation tool to install the inserts flush with surface
of component.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="300" seq="004"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-300-004-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Replace or Install Bonded Components</title>
<warning><para>the ethyl alcohol and adhesives are very flammable
and can damage your eyes and nose. use the items only in well ventilated
areas away from open flames. flush irritated eyes with water.</para>
</warning>
<warning><para>adhesives are toxic and flammable. use only in well
ventilated area and away from open flame. avoid prolonged or repeated
contact with skin or inhalation of vapors. use shop safety precaution
for handling flammable materials.</para></warning>
<caution><para>do not use crocus cloth on aluminum or aluminum alloy
parts. crocus cloth contains an iron oxide which can quickly oxidize
aluminum.</para></caution>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove loose or damaged components. Abrade
all metal surfaces with medium grit aluminum oxide abrasive cloth
or crocus cloth for steel parts.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Clean component and bonding surface with
clean, lint-free cloths and ethyl alcohol to remove any adhesive and
other contaminants. Wipe the part dry before solvent evaporates. Wear
gloves to handle cleaned components.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Install <revst>hook or loop tape<revend> on
back structure assemblies as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove protective backing from <revst>hook
or loop tape<revend>.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Position <revst>hook or loop tape<revend> on
the respective surfaces of back structure assemblies and bond the <revst>hook
or loop tape<revend> in place. Rub with consistent pressure and remove
any air bubbles.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Apply a continuous bead of DP100 adhesive
around edges of <revst>hook or loop tape<revend>.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove excess adhesive with clean, lint-free
cloths and ethyl alcohol. Wipe the part dry before solvent evaporates.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Allow adhesive to cure according to manufacturer&rsquo;s
instructions.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="300" seq="005"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-300-005-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Touch-Up Paint</title>
<warning><para>primer and paint are toxic and flammable. use only
in well ventilated area and away from open flame. avoid prolonged
or repeated contact with skin or inhalation of vapors. use shop safety
precaution for handling flammable materials.</para></warning>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Open Touch-Up Paint Kit and select appropriate
brush tip.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Place selected brush tip on paint applicator.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Pull slider to bottom of paint applicator.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Press down on brush and squeeze applicator
until brush is saturated with paint.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Touch-up the area requiring paint.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="300" seq="006"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-300-006-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Repainting Procedure</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>After damaged area has been repaired, sand
the area to be painted with medium grit aluminum oxide abrasive cloth
or crocus cloth for steel parts.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Mask an area larger than the sanded section
to prevent over-spray.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Select appropriate paint materials from <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-24-19-94a-002-a01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Apply primer, topcoat paint and clear coat,
as appropriate. Follow manufacturer&rsquo;s instructions for cure
times and handling.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="300" seq="007"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-300-007-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Repair of Minor Nicks, Scratches and Corrosion</title>
<caution><para>do not use crocus cloth on aluminum or aluminum alloy
parts. crocus cloth contains an iron oxide which can quickly oxidize
aluminum.</para></caution>
<caution><para>corrosion removing compound is toxic. use only in well
ventilated area. avoid prolonged or repeated contact with skin or
inhalation of vapors.</para></caution>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Use corrosion removing compound to remove
corrosion from metal parts.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Polish out minor nicks or scratches in steel
parts with a crocus cloth.</para>
<note><para>Burrs, nicks and scratches are defined as any material
lifted above the surface of the part. Burrs, nicks and scratches shall
be polished, taking care not to impair form, fit or function. Surface
coat must be replaced after polishing.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Polish out minor burrs, nicks and scratches
in aluminum parts with an aluminum oxide abrasive cloth.</para>
<note><para>During and after cleaning, make sure not to touch surface
to be refinished with hands or allow any grease, oil, etc., to contaminate
the surface.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Clean repaired parts per <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="pgblk-25-24-19-4000"></refint> section.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<warning><para>the chemical film is very flammable and can irritate
eyes and nose. use the chemical film only in well ventilated areas
away from open flames. wear rubber gloves, apron and goggles. do not
let the solution touch eyes or body.</para></warning>
<para>Apply a large quantity of undiluted chemical film. Apply as
many coats as needed to completely cover any bare metal. Permit a
1-minute reaction time between applications.</para>
<note><para>Apply the chemical film with an acid-resistant brush,
swab, synthetic sponge or portable spray equipment. The chemical film
will repair the finish more quickly when the chemical film and the
part are at room temperature, 65 to 75°F (18 to 24°C). Normally, 1
to 5 minutes is necessary for the repair finish to show.</para></note>
<note><para>Chemical film is available in color or clear finish.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove unwanted chemical film with clean
water and lint-free cloths.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="300" seq="005"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="6000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-300-008-a01" revdate="20260918"><revst>
<title><revst>Rivets<revend></title>
<revend>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><revst><para>Permissible limitations on dimension
of rivet holes, where rivets were drilled out on disassembly are determined
by the original design. Rivet type and size cannot be substituted.
Cracked and/or sheared rivets are not acceptable.</para>
<note><para>If a rivet hole appears larger than the defined rivet
or visibly canted, the part must be replaced.</para></note>
<note><para>The minimum pitch and edge distances for rivets are determined
by the original design. Closely monitor during repair.</para></note>
<revend></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
</pgblk>
<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" pgblknbr="7000" chg="r"
key="pgblk-25-24-19-7000" revdate="20260918"><?Pub Dtl>
<chgdesc>Updated to reflect the new logo and name of the company.</chgdesc>
<chgdesc>Updated velcro to hook or loop tape.</chgdesc>
<chgdesc>Updated manufacturer's name.</chgdesc>
<chgdesc>Updated assembly procedures.</chgdesc>
<title>ASSEMBLY</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="99F" seq="010"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-99f-010-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Assembly</title>
<topic>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="99F" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-99f-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>General Information</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>This section contains instructions and notes
needed to prevent damage to the components and possible injury during
assembly of the first class double seat assembly.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Refer to REPAIR to replace threaded inserts
and bonded <revst>hook or loop tape<revend> and cap. Install the attaching
parts given in the IPL to secure all other components.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="94A" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-94a-002-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Materials and Tools</title>
<topic>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="94A" seq="005"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-94a-005-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Consumable Materials</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The consumable materials needed for assembly
are listed in Table <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="table-25-24-19-94a-003-a01"></refint>.</para>
<note><para>Equivalent substitutes may be used for the items listed.</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="94A" seq="003"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" id="table-25-24-19-94a-003-a01">
<title>Consumable Materials</title>
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="col1">
<colspec colname="col2">
<colspec colname="col3">
<thead>
<row>
<entry align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Material Name and Number</para>
</entry>
<entry align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Source</para>
</entry>
<entry align="center"><?Pub _cellfont Weight="bold">
<para>Use</para>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry>
<para> PLT3S-M, Ties, Cable</para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para><revst>Safran Seats USA LLC (V3K723)<revend></para>
</entry>
<entry>
<para>To secure the recline control cable.</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="94B" seq="005"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-94b-005-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Special Tools</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>No special tools are needed for these Assembly
procedures.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="400" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-400-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Seat Assembly Procedures</title>
<topic>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="400" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-400-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Seat Assembly</title>
<caution><para>the first class double seat assembly has covers that
are easily damaged. cover the surfaces and handle the unit with care
to prevent damage.</para></caution>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the base frame assembly (1035) as
follows (<revst>7-1<revend>):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the center spreader assemblies (395
and 390) as follows (<revst>9-1 and 9-1A<revend>):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the helicoils (60 and 55) to aisle
or outboard center spreaders (65 or -65A).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the nut plate (45) to aisle or outboard
center spreaders (65 or -65A) and attach with rivets (50).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the shaft assembly (30) in aisle
or outboard center spreaders (65 or -65A) and attach with helicoil
(40) and setscrew (35).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the seat belt studs (20) and spacers
(25) to aisle or outboard center spreaders (65 or -65A).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the pivot arm (<revst>-5 thru -6A<revend>)
to aisle or outboard center spreaders (65 or -65A) and attach with
helicoils (15), <revst>spacers (13 or -13A), washer (12), bolt (11)
and screws (-10).<revend></para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Connect center spreader assemblies (395 and
390, IPL Figure 7) to rear and front tube assembly (420 and 415) and
attach with washers (410), screws (405) and rivets (-400).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the bottom closeout armrest panels
(380 and 375) between center spreader assemblies (395 and 390) and
attach with rivets (-385).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the outboard and aisle spreader
assemblies (340 and 185) as follows (<revst>8-1 and 8-1A<revend>):</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the helicoils (75,70 and 65) to aisle
or outboard spreader (80 or -80A).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the nut plate (55) to aisle or outboard
spreader (80 or -80A) and attach with rivets (60).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install <revst>loop tape<revend> (50) on
the rubatex bumper (45).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install rubatex bumper (45) to aisle or outboard
spreader (80 or -80A).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the shaft assembly (30) in aisle
or outboard spreader (80 or -80A) and attach with helicoil (40) and
setscrew (35).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the seat belt studs (20) and spacers
(25) to aisle or outboard spreader (80 or -80A).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the pivot arm (<revst>-5 thru -5C<revend>)
to aisle or outboard spreader (80 or -80A) and attach with helicoils
(15), <revst>spacers (13 or -13A), washer (12), bolt (11) and screws
(-10).<revend></para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the forward outboard fitting adapter
(370, IPL Figure 7) to outboard spreader assembly (340).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Connect spreader assembly (340) to rear and
front tube assemblies (420 and 415) and attach with washers (365 and
350), screws (360), bolt (355) and nut (345).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the aft fitting adapter assembly
(315) to outboard spreader assembly (340) and attach with washers
(335), bolts (330 and 325) and nut (320).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the outboard track fitting (290)
to aft fitting adapter assembly (315) and attach with grommets (310),
washers (305 and 300) and bolt (295).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the outboard trunnion (285) and outboard
anti-rattle stud assembly (280) to forward fitting adapter (370).</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para><revst>Install the setscrew (-286) to the
trunion assembly.<revend></para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the leg (255) to rear and front tube
assemblies (420 and 415) and attach with bolts (275 and 270), washers
(265) and nuts (260).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the aisle trunnion (250) and aisle
anti-rattle stud assembly (245) to leg (255). </para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para><revst>Install the setscrew (-251) to the
trunion assembly.<revend></para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the aisle track fitting (215) to
leg (255) and attach with grommets (240), screw (235), washers (230
and 225) and cap nut (220).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Connect aisle spreader assembly (185) to
rear and front tube assemblies (420 and 415) and attach with washers
(210 and 195), screws (205), bolt (200) and nut (190).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the center armrest stanchion (170)
to center spreader assemblies (395 and 390) and attach with washers
(180) and screws (175).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the outboard and aisle stanchion
assemblies (160 and 155) to outboard and aisle spreader assemblies
(340 and 185) and attach with screws (165).</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para><revst>Install the helicoil insert (-166
thru -168) to the outboard and aisle stanchion assemblies.<revend></para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the outboard and aisle pusher assemblies
(140 and 135) to outboard and aisle stanchion assemblies (160 and
155) and attach with washers (150) and screws (145).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the aisle bracket assembly (120)
to aisle stanchion assembly (155) and attach with washers (130) and
screws (125).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the support bumper assembly (105)
to aisle stanchion assembly (155) and to aisle spreader assembly (185)
and attach with screws (115 and 110).</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para><revst>Install the helicoil insert (-116)
to the support bumper assembly.<revend></para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the slide assemblies (100) to spreader
assemblies (395, 390, 340 and 185).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the baggage bar splice assembly (85)
to leg (255) and attach with washer (95) and screw (90).</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para><revst>Install the helicoil insert (-96)
to the baggage bar splice assembly.<revend></para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the baggage bar attach bracket assembly
(75) to aisle spreader assembly (185) and attach with screw (80).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the aisle baggage bar (55) as follows: </para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install aisle baggage bar (55) to baggage
bar splice assembly (85) and attach with washer (70) and screw (65).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install aisle baggage bar (55) to baggage
bar attach bracket assembly (75) and attach with screws (60).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the baggage bar attach plate (30)
to front tube assembly (415) and attach with bolts (45), washers (40)
and nuts (35).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the wall baggage bar (5) as follows:</para>
</prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the wall baggage bar (5) to T bracket
(50) and the baggage bar attach plate (30) and attach with screws
(25), washers (20) and nuts (15).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the wall baggage bar (5) to baggage
bar splice assembly (85) and attach with pin (10).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Assemble the First Class Double Seat assembly
as follows (<revst>1-1 and 1-1A<revend>):</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the foodtable guides assemblies (1025)
to armrest panels (940 and 890) and attach with rivets (-1030).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the outboard and aisle foodtable
guide assemblies (1015 and 1010) to outboard and aisle armrest panels
(920 and 870) and attach with rivets (-1020).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the outboard and aisle foodtable
guide assemblies (1000 and 995) to outboard and aisle inner armrest
panels (940 and 890) and attach with rivets (-1005).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the center armrest panels (970 and
965) and forward closeout armrest panel (985) to base frame assembly
(1035) and attach with rivets (-990, -980 and -975).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the outboard inner armrest panel
(940) and forward closeout armrest (955) to base frame assembly (1035)
and attach with rivets (-960, -950 and -945).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the outboard armrest panel (920)
to base frame assembly (1035) and attach with rivets (-935, -930 and
-925).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the aisle inner armrest panel (890)
and forward closeout armrest (910) to base frame assembly (1035) and
attach with rivets (-915, -905, -900 and -895).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the aisle armrest panel (870) to
base frame assembly (1035) and attach with rivets (-885, -880 and
-875).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the inner shrouds (855 and 850) to
armrest panels (970 and 965) and attach with washers (865) and screws
(860).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the center aft shroud (830) under
base frame assembly (1035) and attach with spacers (845), washers
(840) and screws (835).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the lower shroud (815) under base
frame assembly (1035) and attach with washers (825) and screws (820).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the forward center shroud (800) to
base frame assembly (1035) and attach with washers (810) and screws
(805).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the interface bracket assembly (790)
under base frame assembly (1035) and attach with rivets (-795).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the outboard shroud (775) to outboard
armrest panel (920) and attach with washers (785) and screws (780).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the inner with recline hole shroud
(760) to outboard inner armrest panel (940) and attach with washers
(770) and screws (765).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the forward outboard shroud (745)
to base frame assembly (1035) and attach with washers (755) and screws
(750).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install interface shroud (725) to outboard
inner armrest panel (940) and attach with washers (740) and screws
(735 and 730).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the aisle inner shroud (700) and
bottom support armrest (720) to aisle inner armrest panel (890) and
attach with washers (715) and screws (-710 and 705).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the aisle shroud (685) to aisle armrest
panel (870) and attach with washers (695) and screws (690).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the aisle forward shroud (670) to
base frame assembly (1035) and attach with washers (680) and screws
(675).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the cable assemblies (660) to armrest
panels (970 and 965).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install  the arm center trims (640 and 635)
to base frame assembly (1035) and attach with washers (655) and bolts
(650 and 645).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install  the outboard and aisle arm trims
(625 and 620) to base frame assembly (1035) and attach with screws
(630).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install  the outboard and aisle hinged arm
trims (580 and 575) and mount tabs (615, 610, 605 and 600) to base
frame assembly (1035) and attach with screws (595, 590 and 585).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the cart bumper (560) to aisle shroud
(685) and attach with screws (570 and 565).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the back structure assemblies (535
and 530) as follows (<revst>6-1 and 6-1A<revend>):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para><revst>Install the literature pocket spring
(-116) to the spring mount assemblies (50) with washers (-117) and
screws (-118).<revend></para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the spring block assembly (110) and
monitor mount bracket assemblies (100 and 95) to welded back structure
(155) and attach with rivets (-115 and -105).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install <revst>hook tape (80 thru -85A) <revend>on
back pan (90).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the slide track (70) to welded back
structure (155) and attach with screws (75).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the track stop (60) to slide track
(70) and attach with screws (65).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para><revst>Install the directional studs (56)
to the back pan (90) with washers (57) and rivets (58).<revend></para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the mount spring (50) to pan back
(90) and attach with rivets (-55).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the back pivot brackets (35 and 30)
to back seat filler (150) and attach with washers (45) and bolts (40).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the edge trim neoprene rubber (25)
to back pivot bracket (30).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the quadrants (10 or -10A and 5)
to back pivot brackets (35 and 30) and attach with washers (20) and
bolts (15).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the back structures assemblies (535
and 530, IPL Figure 1) to base frame assembly (1035) and attach with
back pivot studs (555), washers (550 and 545) and pins (540).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the trunnion pins (525) to base frame
assembly (1035).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the recline actuators (510) to trunnion
pins (525) and attach with washers (520) and nuts (515) as show in
Figure <refint reftype="ELEMENT" refid="graphic-25-24-19-440-009-a01"></refint>.
</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Connect the actuator guard (505) to cable
assemblies (660).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the life vest pan (490) to base frame
assembly (1035) and attach with washers (500) and screws (495).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install  the life vest pouch assemblies (470)
to life vest pan (490) and attach with screws (485), washers (480)
and nuts (475).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the seat bottom assemblies (445
and 440) as follows (<revst>5-1 and 5-1A<revend>):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the <revst>hook tape<revend> (71)
on seat bottom pan (75).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the spreaders (60 and 55) under seat
bottom panel (75) and attach with rivets (65), <revst>washer (-65)
as follows:<revend></para></prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para><revst>Install the nutplates (-68) to the
spreader structures with rivets (-69 and -69A) and spreader (-70 or
-70A).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Install the bushings (-67) to the spreader
structures.<revend></para></prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the tubes (45) to spreaders (55 and
60) and attach with screws (50).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the rear tube (35 or -35A) to spreaders
(60 and 55) and attach with screws (40).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the stop assembly (15) to rear tube
assemblies (35 or -35A) and attach with screws (30), washers (25)
and nuts (20).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the track guides (5) to spreaders
(60 and 55) and attach with screws (10).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the seat bottom assemblies (445 and
440, IPL Figure 1) to base frame assembly (1035), back structure assemblies
(535 and 530) and recline actuator (510) and attach with bolts (465
and 460), washers (455) and nuts (450).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Connect the cable assembly (660) to recline
actuator (510) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Connect lock clips of the cable assemblies
(660) to recline actuators (510) as show in Figure <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="graphic-25-24-19-440-009-a01"></refint>.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Route cable assemblies (660) on base frame
assembly (1035) as shown in Figure <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="graphic-25-24-19-440-005-a01"></refint> and attach with cable
ties (665).</para>
<note><para>Make sure recline actuators (510, IPL Figure 1) are positioned
correctly before installing bottom seat assemblies (Refer to Figure <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="graphic-25-24-19-440-009-a01"></refint>).</para>
</note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble the in-arm table assemblies (430
and 425) as follows (<revst>4-1 thru 4-1C<revend>):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the sliding table (<revst>70 thru
-70C<revend>) to table (85 or -85A) and attach with hinges (80),<revst> setsctrew
(-74)<revend> and pins (75).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the slide guides (60), <revst>washer
(-61)<revend> and slides (50) to support (<revst>65 thru -65C<revend>)
and attach with screws (55).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the foodtable support assembly (<revst>40
thru -40C<revend>) to sliding table (<revst>70 thru -70C<revend>)
and attach with screws (45).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the helicoil (-30 and -31), bushing
(25) and tray insert (20) to foodtable pivot (<revst>35 and -35A)
and pivot fittings (-36 and -36A).<revend></para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the foodtable pivot assembly (<revst>5
thru -5C<revend>) to foodtable support assembly (<revst>40 thru -40C<revend>)
and attach with setscrew (10) and pin (15).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install  the in-arm table assemblies (<revst>425
thru -430A<revend>, IPL Figure 1) to base frame assembly (1035) and
attach with pins (<revst>-426 and<revend> 435).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and install the audio jack installation
(400) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install audio plugs (420) to audio jack bracket
assemblies (405).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install audio jack bracket assemblies (405)
to base frame assembly (1035) and attach with washers (415) and screws
(410).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para> Assemble and install PC power port outlet
installation (370) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install double power outlet bezel (375) to
double bracket bezel mount (385) and attach with rivets (-380).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para> Install PC power provisions outlet installation
(370) to base frame assembly (1035) and outboard forward shroud (745)
and attach with washers (395) and screws (390).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para> Install the center aft armcap assembly (355)
to base frame assembly (1035) and attach with screws (365 and 360).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the outboard and aisle aft armcap
assemblies (<revst>340 and 340A<revend>) to base frame assembly (1035)
and attach with screws (350).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the center escutcheon (330) to base
frame assembly (1035) and attach with screws (335).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>install  the outboard and aisle escutcheon
(<revst>315 and 315A<revend>) to base frame assembly (1035) and attach
with screws (325).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install tab (300) to bezel closeout PCU (295)
and attach with washers (310) and screws (305).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Connect bezel closeout PCU (295) to center
armcap assemblies (280 or 280A).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the center armcap assembly (280 or
280A) to center arm trims (640 and 635) and attach with washers (290)
and screws (285).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and install the outboard and aisle
armcap installation (240 and 200) as follows: </para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the hinge tabs (<revst>255A<revend>,
255, <revst>215A<revend> and 215) to armcap assemblies (245 and 205)
and attach with spring torsions (275 and 235), hinge pins (270 and
230) and setscrews (265 and 225).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the armcap assemblies (245 and 205)
to outboard and aisle hinged arm trims (580 and 575) and attach with
bolts (250 and 210).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the lap belt assemblies (195) and
seat belt cover assemblies (190) to seat belt studs (20, IPL Figures
8 and 9) as show in Figure <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="graphic-25-24-19-440-017-a01"></refint>.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the back dress cover assemblies (185,
IPL Figure 1) to back structure assemblies (535 and 530).</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and install double seat assembly
IFE installation (1 or 1A, IPL Figure 3) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Route PCU cable assembly (90) to base frame
assembly (1035, IPL Figure 1) and back structure assemblies (535 and
530) and attach with cable ties (95, IPL Figure 3).</para>
<note><para>Connect PCU cable assembly (90) and cable wrap (100) to
SVDU and DPCU.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install audio jack assemblies (85 and 80)
to inner shrouds (855 and 850, IPL Figure 1).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Assemble and install double wire harness
installations (-40 or -40A, IPL Figure 3) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Install plastic edging grommets (75) to back
structure assemblies (535 and 530, IPL Figure 1).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Route double IFE cable assembly (55, IPL
Figure 3) to base frame assembly (1035, IPL Figure 1) and back structure
assemblies (535 and 530) and attach with cable ties (60, IPL Figure
3).</para>
<note><para>Connect double IFE cable assembly (55) and cable wrap
(45) to audio jack assembly (85) and SVDU.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Install <revst>hook tape<revend> conduits
(50 or -50A) on back structure assemblies (535 and 530, IPL Figure
1).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install USB coupler (30, IPL Figure 3) to
video monitor installation (175, IPL Figure 1) and attach with screws
(35, IPL Figure 3).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Connect USB cable (25) to USB coupler (30)
and SVDU.</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Route double&nbsp;PC power cable assembly
(15) to base frame assembly (1035, IPL Figure 1).</para>
<note><para>Connect double&nbsp;PC power cable assembly (15, IPL Figure
3) and cable wrap (10) to PC power outlet installation (370, IPL Figure
1) and interface bracket assembly (790).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Connect A/C outlet unit (5, IPL Figure 3)
to forward center shroud (800, IPL Figure 1).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and install video monitor installation
(175) as follows (<revst>2-1 and 2-1A<revend>):</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install monitor bezel (60) to monitor dummy
assembly (45) or SVDU (45A) and attach with washers (70) and screws
(65).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install monitor dummy assembly (45) or SVDU
(45A) to monitor bracket assembly (30) and attach with washers (55)
and screws (50).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install monitor bracket assembly (30) to
monitor mount bracket assemblies (100 and 95, IPL Figure 6) and attach
with washers (40, IPL Figure 2) and screws (35).</para></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install monitor shroud assembly (5) to back
structure assemblies (535 and 530, IPL Figure 1) and attach with washers
(15, IPL Figure 2) and screws (10).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the literature pocket assemblies
(145, IPL Figure 1) to back structure assemblies (535 and 530) and
attach with washers (155) and screws (150).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install coat hook mounting block (130) to
back structure assemblies (535 and 530) and attach with washers (140)
and screws (135).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install coat hook (120) to coat hook mounting
block (130) and attach with screws (125).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Assemble and install the headrest assembly
(40) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Assemble and install the headrest structure
assembly (65) as follows:</para></prcitem>
<prclist4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Install the hinge assemblies (90) to side
panel assemblies (110 and 105) and center panel assemblies (115) and
attach with washers (100) and screws (95).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
<prcitem4><prcitem><para>Install the slide block (70) to headrest
structure assembly (65) and attach with ball plungers (85), washers
(80) and screws (75).</para></prcitem></prcitem4>
</prclist4>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the center cushion (60) to headrest
structure assembly (65).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the side cushion (55 and 50) to headrest
structure assembly (65).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Install the headrest dress cover (-45) to
headrest structure assembly (65).</para></prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the back upholstered assembly (25)
to back structure assemblies (535 and 530).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Install the bottom upholstered assembly (10)
to seat bottom assemblies (445 and 440).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
<graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="440" seq="009"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="graphic-25-24-19-440-009-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Recline Actuator Installation</title>
<sheet gnbr="I-252419-07001-1-1" sheetnbr="1" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-24-19-440-009-a01-1" revdate="20080417"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="040" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-040-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Recline Cable Adjustments</title>
<note><para>If the recline button (Refer to Figure <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="graphic-25-24-19-440-016-a01"></refint>)
does not have a firm feel and does not return to the normal position,
one of the recline cable ends might be improperly seated in position.
Check both ends of the recline cable (at input assembly and output
assembly ends) to ensure that each cable end is properly seated.</para>
</note>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If necessary, loosen jam nut securing output
adjustment nut (Refer to Figure <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="graphic-25-24-19-440-009-a01"></refint>) and unscrew adjustment
nut so that there are three to four threads exposed between the jam
nut and cable sheath.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Loosely tighten jam nut.</para>
<note><para>If the back structure will not recline, the recline cable
is too tight. If the recline actuator does not firmly lock the back
structure in place, the recline cable is too loose.</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Press recline button and recline back structure.
Verify that the back structure will recline smoothly without binding.
If binding is noticed, remove back structure from base frame, check
all parts and reassemble.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If back structure does not recline, loosen
jam nut and readjust recline cable output adjustment nut to loosen
recline cable. Loosely tighten jam nut and repeat step 2.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Release recline button and verify that back
structure locks firmly in place.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>If back structure does not lock firmly in
place, loosen jam nut and readjust recline cable output adjustment
nut to tighten recline actuator cable. Loosely tighten jam nut and
repeat step 5.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>When proper adjustment is completed, firmly
tighten jam nut against output adjustment nut, taking care not to
move output adjustment nut. Repeat steps 1 through 7 to verify that
adjustment is correct.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="040" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-040-002-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Full Upright and Recline Adjustments</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Remove the bottom cushion assembly to access
recline actuators.</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the bottom cushion assembly to access
recline actuators.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Remove the back cushion assembly to access
back structure assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Press the recline buttons (Refer to Figure <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="graphic-25-24-19-440-016-a01"></refint>)
and move back structures to full upright position.</para>
<note><para>The full upright position must be 23.4 in. (59.43 cm)
from vertical reference (Refer to Figure <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="graphic-25-24-19-440-016-a01"></refint>).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use bottom of leg to obtain a horizontal
plane (Refer to Figure <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="graphic-25-24-19-440-016-a01"></refint>) and measure the vertical
angle of seat back assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Adjust the jam nuts that secure recline actuators
to trunnion pins. Refer to Figure <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="graphic-25-24-19-440-009-a01"></refint>. Tighten both jam nuts
against trunnion pins.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Press recline buttons (Refer to Figure <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="graphic-25-24-19-440-016-a01"></refint>)
and move back structures to full recline position.</para>
<note><para>The full recline position must be 28.8 in. (73.15 cm)
from vertical reference (Refer to Figure <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="graphic-25-24-19-440-016-a01"></refint>).</para></note>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use bottom of leg to obtain a horizontal
plane (Refer to Figure <refint reftype="ELEMENT"
refid="graphic-25-24-19-440-016-a01"></refint>) and measure the recline
angle of seat back assembly.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Loosen setscrew (Refer to Figure <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="graphic-25-24-19-440-009-a01"></refint>)
on recline actuator and turn ring to achieve 28.8 in. (73.15 cm) of
recline. Tighten setscrew and place a torque strip on ring once full
recline angle is achieved.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
<graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="440" seq="005"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="graphic-25-24-19-440-005-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Recline Cable Routing</title>
<sheet gnbr="I-252419-07001-2-1" sheetnbr="1" chg="n"
key="sheet-25-24-19-440-005-a01-1" revdate="20260918"></sheet>
</graphic><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="440"
seq="017" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="graphic-25-24-19-440-017-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Y-lap Belt Installation</title>
<sheet gnbr="I-252419-07001-3-1" sheetnbr="1" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-24-19-440-017-a01-1" revdate="20080417"></sheet>
</graphic><graphic chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="440"
seq="016" confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="7000" chg="u"
key="graphic-25-24-19-440-016-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Full Upright Position and Full Recline Position Adjustments</title>
<sheet gnbr="I-252419-07001-4-1" sheetnbr="1" chg="u"
key="sheet-25-24-19-440-016-a01-1" revdate="20080417"></sheet>
</graphic></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
</pgblk>
<pgblk chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" pgblknbr="8000" chg="r"
key="pgblk-25-24-19-8000" revdate="20260918"><?Pub Dtl>
<chgdesc>Updated to reflect the new logo and name of the company.</chgdesc>
<title>FITS AND CLEARANCES</title>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="99F" seq="011"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="8000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-99f-011-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>General Information For Fits and Clearances</title>
<topic>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="99F" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="8000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-99f-002-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>General Information</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>This section gives dimensional information
to let the technician find if the assembly is serviceable or make
a decision about the level of repair that is necessary.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</subtask>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="700" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="8000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-700-002-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Torque Limits</title>
<topic>
<subtask chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="700" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="8000" chg="u"
key="subtask-25-24-19-700-001-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Assembly Torque Limits</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The Assembly Torque Limits in Table <refint
reftype="ELEMENT" refid="table-25-24-19-820-001-a01"></refint> gives
applicable torque limits for all critical fasteners. The torque values
are shown in the English (inch-pounds) standard value followed by
the Metric (N&bull;m) equivalent in parentheses.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="820" seq="001"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="8000" id="table-25-24-19-820-001-a01">
<title>Assembly Torque Limits</title>
<tgroup cols="5">
<colspec colname="col1">
<colspec colname="col2">
<colspec colname="col3">
<colspec colname="col4">
<colspec colname="col5">
<thead>
