<ipl chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" pgblknbr="10000" chg="r"
key="ipl-25-24-19" revdate="20260918"><?Pub Dtl>
<chgdesc>Updated to reflect the new logo and name of the company.</chgdesc>
<chgdesc>Updated numerical index to reflect revision 1.</chgdesc>
<chgdesc>Added new vendor details.</chgdesc>
<chgdesc>Updated manufacturer's name.</chgdesc>
<chgdesc>Updated REPLD and REPLS to RPLD and RPLS.</chgdesc>
<title>ILLUSTRATED PARTS LIST (IPL)</title>
<iplintro>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="99F" seq="012"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="10000" chg="u"
key="task-25-23-24-99f-012-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Scope of Information</title>
<topic>
<title>Introduction</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>General</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Each assembly is recorded and immediately
followed by a record of its detail parts. The record is indentured
to show the difference between each part and the higher assembly.
Item numbers in the parts list agree with the item numbers of the
included illustration (figure).</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>How to Identify a Part</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>When the part number is known, find the part
number in the index. Record the figure and item number. Find the item
number in the applicable parts list and illustration to get the necessary
data.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>When the part number is not known, look at
the illustrations to identify the part by shape and location. Refer
to the included parts list to get the PART NUMBER, NOMENCLATURE, EFFECTIVITY
and QUANTITY.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Use the EFFECTIVITY CODE to show the use
of a part to its higher assembly. When the EFFECTIVITY CODE column
is empty, the use of the part applies to all NEXT-HIGHER-ASSEMBLIES
unless specified differently in the NOMENCLATURE column.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="99F" seq="013"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="10000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-99f-013-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Equipment Designator Index</title>
<topic>
<title>General</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The EQUIPMENT DESIGNATOR INDEX is an aid
to find the parts in the DETAIL PARTS LIST by the EQUIPMENT DESIGNATOR.
Each entry gives the EQUIPMENT DESIGNATOR, the PART NUMBER, the FIGURE
NUMBER and the ITEM NUMBER.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Put the EQUIPMENT DESIGNATOR INDEX in sequence,
one character at a time, from left to right. The correct sequence
is (1) dash, (2) letters A through Z and (3) numerals 0 through 9.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="99F" seq="014"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="10000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-99f-014-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Numerical Index</title>
<topic>
<title>General</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The NUMERICAL INDEX is an aid to find parts
in the DETAIL PARTS LIST by part number. It gives the FIGURE NUMBER,
the ITEM NUMBER and the TOTAL QUANTITY REQUIRED for each entry.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Put the PART NUMBERS in sequence, one character
at a time, from left to right. The correct sequence is (1) dash, (2)
letters A through Z and (3) numerals 0 through 9.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
<task chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="99F" seq="015"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="10000" chg="u"
key="task-25-24-19-99f-015-a01" revdate="20080417">
<title>Explanation of Detail Parts List Entries</title>
<topic>
<title>General</title>
<prclist1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>The DETAIL PARTS LIST is the general sequence
of disassembly. Illustrate the parts and record them in the related
parts list.</para></prcitem></prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>FIG. ITEM Column</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>The first number at the top of each FIG.
ITEM column is the figure number of the exploded-view illustration.
The number given opposite each part number is the item number given
to the part in the illustration.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>A dash (-) in front of an item number shows
that the part is not illustrated.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Alpha-variants A through Z (except I and
O) are given to item numbers when necessary to identify added parts,
alternate parts and parts changed by service bulletins.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>PART NUMBER Column</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>This column gives the part number of the
manufacturer for each part, as changed to meet the requirements of
ATA 200/2000. The changes can include:</para></prcitem>
<prclist3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><title>Removal of empty spaces and special characters.
Dashes are permitted only between number characters.</title></prcitem>
</prcitem3>
<prcitem3><prcitem><para>Add a reference part number that agrees with
ATA 200/2000 if the PART NUMBER is longer than 15 characters. In these
cases, give the full part number in the NOMENCLATURE column.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem3>
</prclist3>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>Identure Column</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>The indenture column shows how parts are
related. A typical relation is as follows:</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<table chapnbr="25" sectnbr="24" subjnbr="19" func="99A" seq="002"
confltr="A" varnbr="01" pgblknbr="10000" frame="none"
id="table-25-24-19-99a-002-a01">
<tgroup cols="8">
<?PubTbl tgroup cbmarg="1.00px" ctmarg="1.00px">
<colspec colname="col1" colwidth="1.64*">
<colspec colname="col2" colwidth="10.00px">
<colspec colname="colspec5" colwidth="10.00px">
<colspec colname="colspec4" colwidth="10.00px">
<colspec colname="colspec3" colwidth="10.00px">
<colspec colname="colspec2" colwidth="0.19cm">
<colspec colname="colspec1" colwidth="3.13*">
<colspec colname="colspec0" colwidth="3.31*">
<tbody>
<row>
<entry morerows="6" colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify"></entry>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify">
<para>1</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify">
<para>2</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify">
<para>3</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify">
<para>4</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify"></entry>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify"></entry>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify"></entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify">
<para>*</para>
</entry>
<entry namest="colspec5" nameend="colspec0" colsep="0" rowsep="0"
align="justify">
<para>Assembly</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify">
<para>*</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify">
<para>*</para>
</entry>
<entry namest="colspec4" nameend="colspec0" colsep="0" rowsep="0"
align="justify">
<para>Detailed parts for assembly</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify">
<para>*</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify">
<para>*</para>
</entry>
<entry namest="colspec4" nameend="colspec0" colsep="0" rowsep="0"
align="justify">
<para>Sub- assembly</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify">
<para>*</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify">
<para>*</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify">
<para>*</para>
</entry>
<entry namest="colspec3" nameend="colspec0" colsep="0" rowsep="0"
align="justify">
<para>Detailed parts for sub-assembly</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify">
<para>*</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify">
<para>*</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify">
<para>*</para>
</entry>
<entry namest="colspec3" nameend="colspec0" colsep="0" rowsep="0"
align="justify">
<para>Sub-sub-assembly</para>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<?PubTbl row rht="0.29in">
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify">
<para>*</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify">
<para>*</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify">
<para>*</para>
</entry>
<entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="justify">
<para>*</para>
</entry>
<entry namest="colspec2" nameend="colspec0" colsep="0" rowsep="0"
align="justify">
<para>Detailed parts for sub-sub-assembly</para>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<?Pub _newpage>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>NOMENCLATURE Column</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>This column gives descriptive nomenclature
for each part. It can also give the CAGE code of the manufacturer
(<revst>if the part is not made by SSUSA<revend>), the part number
(if it is longer than 15 digits or changed to ATA 200/2000), a service
bulletin that changes the part and expired part numbers. The column
also gives the figure for NHA and more data as necessary.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>Record both the pre- and post-service bulletin
configurations of assemblies, subassemblies and detail parts subjected
to modification, deletion, addition or replacement by an issued service
bulletin. The term (PRE SB XXXX) in the NOMENCLATURE column identifies
the initial configuration and the term (POST SB XXXX) identifies assemblies
and parts after the change is completed.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>When applicable, use the terms defined below
to indicate the interchangeability of parts. These names show how
parts are interchangeable.</para></prcitem></prcitem2>
<prcitem2><prcitem>
<deflist>
<defdata><term>Abbreviation</term><fullterm>Term</fullterm><def>Definition
</def></defdata>
<defdata><term>ALT</term><fullterm>Alternate</fullterm><def>The recorded
part is an alternative to and interchangeable with other parts in
the same item number group or other item numbers when identified.</def>
</defdata>
<defdata><term>SUPSD BY</term><fullterm>Superseded By</fullterm><def>The
part is superseded by and is not interchangeable with the item number
identified in the note.</def></defdata>
<defdata><term>SUPSDS</term><fullterm>Supersedes</fullterm><def>The
part supersedes and is not interchangeable with the item number identified
in the note.</def></defdata>
<defdata><term><revst>RPLD BY<revend></term><fullterm>Replaced By</fullterm>
<def>The part is replaced by and is interchangeable with the item
number identified in the note.</def></defdata>
<defdata><term><revst>RPLS<revend></term><fullterm>Replaces</fullterm>
<def>The part replaces and is interchangeable with the item number
identified in the note.</def></defdata>
</deflist>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<?Pub _newpage>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>EFF CODE Column</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>This column contains effectivity codes (A,
B, etc.) to indicate the alternate models or configurations of the
end items to which the parts apply. This column is left blank when
the parts apply to all models or configurations in the parts list.
When an asterisk (*) is used, the part is contained in a kit which
is listed at the end of the detail parts lists.</para></prcitem>
</prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
<prcitem1><prcitem><para>UNITS PER ASSY Column</para></prcitem>
<prclist2>
<prcitem2><prcitem><para>The quantity shown in this column is the
units required for one next higher assembly (NHA). The abbreviation
RF (reference) means the end item or assembly is shown completely
assembled in the figure referenced in the NOMENCLATURE column.</para>
</prcitem></prcitem2>
</prclist2>
</prcitem1>
</prclist1>
</topic>
</task>
